# This image builds from the lockfile, not from the developer's working tree.
# `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile runs AFTER `RUN npm ci`, so a host node_modules
# would silently overwrite the container's freshly installed, platform-correct
# dependencies with the host's binaries (vite build would then run against
# darwin binaries inside a linux image). A host dist is emptied by the vite
# build anyway and only bloats the context upload. Vite also reads a
# frontend-local .env automatically during build, so anything under that name
# must never ride into the image on a machine that happens to have one.
node_modules
dist
.env
.env.*
